plan_in_issue:
**Goal.** Today the AI search adds one extra line for a payoff that comes later (a countdown, a next-turn reward), under R3696000, and replies to it before the finalists are scored on the other determinizations. That reply spends nodes those worlds need. After this change:
- The extra line is replied to only after every shortlisted line.
- It runs on its own sub-counter, holding only the nodes left after what the finalists' scores on the other worlds keep back. Both of a countdown's replies come out of that sub-counter.
- It is skipped once the host's wrap-up has fired. That builds the "skip on a short clock" that #3696 planned and never built.
- The R3696000 note, §9.9, the R3498000 sentence it contradicts and the AI docs are corrected to match.
- New tests show that on a tight budget the extra line never costs a world its score (`worlds_scored`), and that a fired wrap-up skips it.

